28bn|n|The quality or state of being useful; usefulness; production of good; profitableness to some valuable end; as, the utility of manure upon land; the utility of the sciences; the utility of medicines. ; Adaptation to satisfy the desires or wants; intrinsic value. See Note under Value, 2. ; Happiness; the greatest good, or happiness, of the greatest number, -- the foundation of utilitarianism.	a:1zwk,100,3~1zwk,100,3	n:lfp,103,4~lfp,103,4	N:dk2,115,2;15hp,101,4~15hp,101,4;dk2,115,2
28bv|n|The most that can be; the farthest limit; the greatest power, degree, or effort; as, he has done his utmost; try your utmost.	N:10z4,108,4;b0x,82,3~10z4,108,4;b0x,82,3
